## What the Red role did
- Marked task 1.4a [~] in plan.md.
- Wrote packages/architecture-enforcement/src/__tests__/architecture-analyzer-cost.test.ts
  with the 8 cases of test-strategy section P1.11.
- Seams: a vi.mock("typescript", ...) wrapper counts whole-file forEachChild walks per
  registered fixture path (vi.spyOn cannot hook ts.forEachChild; the namespace defines
  members as getters without configurable). A passthrough vi.mock("../analyzer.js")
  counts analyzeArchitectureSources calls. A passthrough vi.mock("node:child_process")
  counts git archive calls (the projection seam).
- AC-6 fixture: 50 member-access arguments new Client(db.users) against a same-shape
  control with string arguments; growth pair with 10 and 50 nodes.
- AC-6b fixture: one require binding, one await-import binding, one unassigned name,
  and one double declaration. The strict expected list pins first-declaration-wins and
  both assignment forms. One fix during Red: the first fixture table name
  companyAccounts matched a rule without the client-construction kind, so the
  characterization saw zero findings. The fixture now exports reviewJobs, which
  resolves to database-table:review_jobs under DURABLE_JOB_DATABASE_BOUNDARY. This is
  a fixture correction, not a contract change.
- AC-7 fixture: the refresh runs in the test process through runArchitecturePinRefreshCli
  on a fixture built like the pin test base fixture (the whole package src; the fixed
  implementation path lists require it), with a stale manifest clone for the
  acknowledged and the preview run.
- AC-8: the key list before and after the refresh is compared in order, the strict
  sync validator is the oracle, and a control manifest with one extra key is rejected.
- AC-8b: a new analyzed file after the refresh fails the CI-mode check with the report
  hash error and no input snapshot error.
- No test reads clock time. Every count is emitted as label=<n> from a same-named
  variable. The file holds no measure/tracks or measure/runs path.

